From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] advapi32, server: LogonUser checks the password and gives the account's token

LogonUser was a stub. It said yes to any name and any password and handed
back 0xdeadbeef as the token. Programs that check credentials with it (run
as another user, installers, services that log a user on) accepted
anything; programs that used the token crashed or failed.

As on Windows, LogonUser(Ex) now checks the account's password and returns
a token for that account. In a shared prefix this goes through the
elevation broker (sg-session's sg-brokerd, "@logon"):

- advapi32's unix side sends the account and password over the broker's
  socket. The broker's root monitor checks them with PAM, as it does for
  elevation, and on success writes a one-time ticket into a directory only
  the SYSTEM account may read. The ticket names the account, the requester
  and a 30-second limit. The password never reaches the wineserver, a log
  or a file, and both ends wipe it.
- The new server request logon_ticket_token takes the ticket, and only
  when all of these hold: it is owned by the SYSTEM account (or root), no
  one else may read it, it was made for this requester, it has not
  expired, and it is not for root or SYSTEM. The server unlinks it and
  makes a token for the account in the caller's session: a primary token,
  or an impersonation token for a network logon. The caller's handle has
  full access.
- Wrong password, unknown account, root, SYSTEM, or a domain other than
  this machine: ERROR_LOGON_FAILURE. No broker: ERROR_NO_LOGON_SERVERS.
  LOGON32_LOGON_NEW_CREDENTIALS returns the caller's own token, as on
  Windows, which checks those credentials only when they are used.
- In a single-user prefix there is no broker and only one account: the
  caller's own name is accepted on its word, as before, and gets the
  caller's token.
- LogonUserEx returns the logon SID. LogonUserA passed the user name as the
  domain; it now passes the domain.
- GetUserName returns the impersonated user while a thread impersonates,
  as on Windows.
- winbase.h gains the LOGON32_LOGON_* and LOGON32_PROVIDER_* constants.

An older broker refuses the request at once: it carries no program, so it
never reaches a consent prompt.

Gate: test/logonuser-gate.sh (sgsystem, sgtest1, sgtest2, the broker as
root with a stand-in for PAM; SG_SESSION_SRC). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_TICKET_ANY_OWNER, SG_MUTANT_TICKET_ANY_REQUESTER, and
sg-session's SG_MUTANT_LOGON_NO_PASSWORD_CHECK.
